    "q-97196": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97196",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.1),$ compute $P(X=0).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}p, & x=1 \\\\ 1-p, & x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.1),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.1, & x=1 \\\\ 0.9, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=0)=f(0)=0.9.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
