    "q-97185": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97185",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.8)$ and $Y∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.6)$ are independent, calculate $P(X=0\\,\\cap \\,Y=1).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the multiplication law for independent events, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,\\cap \\,Y=1) & =P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.8),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(X=1)=0.8,\\,P(X=0)=0.2,\n$$\n\nand since $Y∼\\text{Bernoulli}(0.6),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=1)=0.6,\\,P(Y=0)=0.4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,\\cap \\,Y=1) & =P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=1) \\\\  & =0.2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0.12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97185-a",
